title: Prototype
---
<<declare $selectedPath = "">>
<<hideallportraits>>
<<wait 8>>
<<showportrait Left Sekhmet>>
<<pulseglow Sekhmet>>
Sekhmet: The <color=red>fate of Egypt</color> is at a <b>crossroads.</b> #expression:neutral
<<showportrait Right Meritamun>>
Meritamun: But what does that mean for me?  #expression:worried
Sekhmet: You will carry messages of the divine will to mortals: <color=red>you are our eyes in the mortal realm.</color> You are to help us guide them to glory. Is that understood? #expression:neutral
Meritamun: I am your vessel, Lady Sekhmet – your will is my desire. #expression:neutral
<<showportrait CenterLeft Bes>>
<<angerreaction Bes>>
Bes: BUT YOU MADE HER INTO A CAT!? 
Bes:I must register my objection here, Sekhmet. 
Bes:Small cats are in the domestic sphere and therefore in MY realm of influence! Felines are for killing snakes around the house! Not for <color=red>whatever THIS is that you’re trying to do!</color> #expression:neutral

<<showportrait Left Sekhmet>>
Sekhmet: I never try, I only <color=red>execute.</color> 
Sekhmet: Look here Meritamun – Lord Bes orders you to be bound by holy decree to <color=red>kill snakes and rats around the Temple.</color> That is also part of our divine will. #expression:neutral

<<showportrait Right Meritamun>>
Meritamun: My joy is the will of the Gods, absolutely. No snakes or rats will besmirch the temple grounds… #expression:neutral

<<hideportrait Left>>
<<hideportrait CenterLeft>>
<<openingdayreveal OpeningDayReveal>>

<<setpuzzle 𓀀𓅱𓄤:Path_A|𓇳𓅓𓁶:Path_B>>
<<showportrait Right Cat_Meritamun>>
Cat_Meritamun: \[Oh! Someone is coming!\] #expression:neutral
Cat_Meritamun: \[I must remember to <color=red>use the heiroglyphs on the wall</color> to communicate the will of the Gods!\]  #expression:pawraised
<<showportrait Left Amenhotep>>
Amenhotep: I ask forgiveness for this small blasphemy...
<<sadreaction Amenhotep>>
Amenhotep: but I feel the holy <color=red>City of Thebes</color> is not the same without <color=red>Meritamun</color> here. 
Amenhotep: My trust in your divine plan wavered on this score, and I came here to this sanctum to unburden myself.  #expression:neutral
Amenhotep: The arrival of a new <color=red>Temple Cat</color> has however eased my sorrow somewhat --
Amenhotep: The local snakes have been feeling the thunder of her paws! 
<<showportrait Right Cat_Meritamun>>
<<playsustainedsound CatPurr>>
Cat_Meritamun: *purrrrrr* #expression:standing
Amenhotep: Meritamun’s <color=red>younger sister Nitiqret</color> is now appointed God’s Wife of Amun. I think she needs your guidance, but is a bit too proud to ask. 
Amenhotep: And of course there is the little child, <color=red>my son.</color>  
Amenhotep: Knots of worry gnaw at me day and night, and so I come to ask your guidance on this – should I : <br> Write <b><size=+4>𓀀</size></b> to our child's <b><size=+4>𓅱</size></b> grandmother <b><size=+4>𓄤</size></b> and ask her for news of our little one? Or <br> would it be much safer to not <b><size=+4>𓇳</size></b> send <b><size=+4>𓅓</size></b> letters <b><size=+4>𓁶</size></b> too often lest he be discovered? #wordsearch
<<if $selectedPath == "Path_A">>
    Amenhotep: I shall write to <color=red>Neferura</color> straight away! 
    <<addgodaffinity Bes 1>> 
    <<addhumanaffinity Chaos 1>>
<<elseif $selectedPath == "Path_B">>
    Amenhotep: It is true that Ahmose's spies are everywhere, <color=red>Neferura</color> and I should be as careful as possible.
    <<addgodaffinity Thoth 1>> 
    <<addhumanaffinity Ptahhotep 1>>
<<endif>>
Cat_Meritamun: \[Amenhotep has a son? How long has it been since I died?\]  #expression:puzzled
<<hideallportraits>>

<<setpuzzle 𓎡𓃀𓂋:Path_A|𓄿𓊹𓉐:Path_B>>

<<showportrait Left Ahmose>>
Ahmose: I’ve placed my <color=red>second daughter Nitiqret</color> here as God’s Wife of Amun and my <color=red>eldest son Harwa</color> to ease her way politically. Both of them here in Thebes, here in your divine care, oh Gods. #expression:neutral
Ahmose: That business with my <color=red>eldest daugther Meritamun</color> needed to be buried, and quickly. 
Ahmose:Honestly I can’t wait to get rid of that rat bastard of a <color=red>high priest Amenhotep</color> but he’s a bit too secure here in Thebes – he has too many connections with the local elite families.
<<showportrait Right Cat_Meritamun>>
<<playsustainedsound CatPurr>>
Cat_Meritamun: *purrrrrr* #expression:puzzled
Ahmose:  But here’s my question to the great divinities that may be in this holy place, would it be wiser to :

Ahmose: Make <b><size=+4>𓎡</size></b> a move <b><size=+4>𓃀</size></b> against <b><size=+4>𓂋</size></b> Amenhotep? Or <br> Let <b><size=+4>𓄿</size></b> him <b><size=+4>𓊹</size></b> be <b><size=+4>𓉐</size></b> and try to work with him remaining in his post as high priest? #wordsearch

<<if $selectedPath == "Path_A">>  
    Ahmose: Yes, yes… As soon as Harwa and Nitiqret are settled here I’m going to oust him. I’ll have to see what I can do to start discrediting him, immediately…
        <<addgodaffinity Sekhmet 1>> 
        <<addhumanaffinity Harwa 1>>

    <<elseif $selectedPath == "Path_B">>
    Ahmose: I suppose that is the safer option, at least until Harwa and Nitiqret are settled here. 
        <<addgodaffinity Bast 1>> 
        <<addhumanaffinity Nitiqret 1>>
<<endif>>
Cat_Meritamun: \[ Oh father! What are you doing\]  #expression:puzzled
<<sadreaction Cat_Meritamun>>
Cat_Meritamun: \[I suppose this is the mess I left behind when I died, and now I have to clean it up. \]  #expression:puzzled 
<<hideallportraits>>

<<setpuzzle 𓏍𓌅𓆣:Path_A|𓇳𓌅𓆣:Path_B>>

<<showportrait Left Harwa>>
Harwa: Chariot race with the boys tomorrow – Lady Sekhmet hear my prayers! #expression:laughing
Harwa: I heard from Amenhotep that <color=red>a desert cat has blessed this holy temple</color> with her grace and fury – and I just know that this is sign that I’ll win tomorrow. #expression:laughing
<<showportrait Right Cat_Meritamun>>
<<playsustainedsound CatPurr>>
Cat_Meritamun: *Purrrrrrr......*
Harwa: Father thinks I’m being an idiot and I’ll get injured, so I told him I'd pray to ask the Gods, so here I am. Should I <br> join <b><size=+4>𓏍</size></b> the race <b><size=+4>𓌅</size></b> tomorrow <b><size=+4>𓆣</size></b>? OR <br> Not <b><size=+4>𓇳</size></b> race <b><size=+4>𓌅</size></b> tomorrow <b><size=+4>𓆣</size></b>? #wordsearch
<<if $selectedPath == "Path_A">>  
    Harwa: The Gods have spoken! Haha! On to victory! #expression:laughing
        <<addgodaffinity Sekhmet 1>> 
        <<addhumanaffinity Chaos 1>>

    <<elseif $selectedPath == "Path_B">>

    Harwa:  Oh well, I suppose wisdom must prevail ... I'll sit this one out, but I WILL still place bets on the other racers...
        <<addgodaffinity Thoth 1>> 
        <<addhumanaffinity Chaos 1>>
<<endif>>
Cat_Meritamun: \[Harwa is a bit taller than I remember, so maybe... <color=red>a year</color> has passed since I left my life here?\]  #expression:puzzled
<<hideallportraits>>
<<fadetonight BackgroundManager>>

<<showportrait Left Thoth>>
Thoth: But dearest you know the <color=red>mortals are often idiots...</color>  
Thoth: ...and if you give them a cat, they may well do exactly as the cat says, but they'll do it exactly the wrong way, so why bother?
<<showportrait CenterLeft Sekhmet>>
<<angerreaction Sekhmet>>
Sekhmet: What even is the POINT of you, <color=red>Thoth</color>, if you can’t use your imagination? 
Sekhmet:And don’t you ‘dearest’ me it’s patronising. If I wanted that kind of self righteous nonsense <color=red>I’d tickle Apep’s balls instead.</color> 
Thoth: ...
<<showportrait Right Meritamun>>
Meritamun: ... #expression:worried
Thoth: Maybe not in front of the <color=red>children?</color>
Sekhmet: ... no I suppose not. Meritamun you heard nothing and weren't here.
Meritamun: Indeed – my Lady and my Lord, I wasn’t here and I heard nothing at all… #expression:worried

<<hideallportraits>>

<<fadetoday BackgroundManager>>

<<setpuzzle 𓐫𓃠𓁷:Path_A|𓋴𓌅𓌢:Path_B>>

<<showportrait Left Nitiqret>>
<<sadreaction Nitiqret>>
Nitiqret: I don’t know why <color=red>my mother has abandoned me.</color> 
Nitiqret: One minute we were <color=red>grieving Meritamun’s</color> passing, together as a family --
Nitiqret: the next minute we're not allowed to talk about Meritamun, and it's like she never even existed?
<<showportrait Right Cat_Meritamun>>
<<playsustainedsound CatPurr>>
Cat_Meritamun: *Purrrrrrr* 
<<sadreaction Nitiqret>>
Nitiqret: I’m so lost. 
Nitiqret: The nobles here hate me and I have literally no clue why. <color=red>Harwa’s</color> doing fine of course, making new friends at court left right and center. 
Nitiqret: .... but actually I came here because I heard a <color=red>cat</color> has come to live here! And here you are!
<<playsustainedsound CatPurr>>
Cat_Meritamun: *PurrrrrrrRRRRRrrrr* 
Nitiqret: Would you like <br> to be given a little <b><size=+4>𓐫</size></b> scritch <b><size=+4>𓃠</size></b> on your head <b><size=+4>𓁷</size></b>? OR <br> would you like to be given a little ride <b><size=+4>𓋴</size></b> on this chariot <b><size=+4>𓌅</size></b> toy <b><size=+4>𓌢</size></b>? #wordsearch

<<if $selectedPath == "Path_A">>
    Nitiqret: Wonderful! I shall pet you gently, and then maybe we can find you a little mouse to play with... #expression:happy
    <<addgodaffinity Bes 1>>
    <<addhumanaffinity Chaos 1>>
<<elseif $selectedPath == "Path_B">>
    Nitiqret: I knew you were a feisty one, just like Lady Sekhment, <color=red>ROAR!</color> #expression:happy
    <<addgodaffinity Sekhmet 1>>
    <<addhumanaffinity Harwa 1>>
<<endif>>
Cat_Meritamun: \[Dear Sweet Nitiqret! I wish you wouldn't let those bitchy nobles get you down!\] #expression:puzzled
<<hideallportraits>>

<<setpuzzle 𓆓𓉻𓋾:Path_A|𓄣𓏛𓈗:Path_B>>

<<showportrait Left Harwa>>
<<angerreaction Harwa>>
Harwa: Gods! I am so sick of losing at the dice table. <color=red>Senemut</color> never seems to lose nearly as much money as I do, I don't know what I'm doing wrong.
<<sadreaction Harwa>>
Harwa: Father says I'm a terrible prince and I need to pray for guidance as to how to conduct myself.
<<showportrait Right Cat_Meritamun>>
<<playsustainedsound CatPurr>>
Cat_Meritamun: *Purrrrrrrr...*
Harwa: So here I am, asking the gods...Should I <br> step <b><size=+4>𓆓</size></b> away <b><size=+4>𓉻</size></b> from <b><size=+4>𓋾</size></b> the dice table? or <br> go back and try to win back my <b><size=+4>𓄣</size></b> previous <b><size=+4>𓏛</size></b> losses <b><size=+4>𓈗</size></b>? #wordsearch

<<if $selectedPath == "Path_A">>
    Harwa: As the Gods wish, I suppose… actually maybe this means I can go back to betting on Chariot races!
    <<addgodaffinity Thoth 1>>
    <<addhumanaffinity Ptahhotep 1>>
<<elseif $selectedPath == "Path_B">>
    Harwa: Yes! I knew the Gods were on my side all along! Ha! #expression:laughing
    <<addgodaffinity Bes 1>>
    <<addhumanaffinity Harwa 1>>
<<endif>>
Cat_Meritamun: \[You know, <color=red>Harwa</color> -- you'd be so much more confident if you just applied yourself to something more difficult than gambling!\] #expression:neutral

<<hideallportraits>>
<<fadetonight BackgroundManager>>
<<showportrait Left Bast>>
Bast: So, <color=red>Meritamun</color> – what is <color=red>your father Pharoah Ahmose</color> going to do about the Persians at the border? Will he sue for peace? 
Bast: Growing up in the shadow of war is a difficult thing for a <color=red>child</color> such as yours, you know…
<<showportrait Right Meritamun>>
Meritamun: I’m sorry my <color=red>Lady Bast</color>, but I confess I am confused – #expression:worried
Meritamun: As I recall, I was by the grace of your blessing, <color=red>with child when I died...</color>
Meritamun: …but the unborn babe <color=red>didn’t survive my own death.</color> #expression:worried
Meritamun: I agree with you, however – war can be hard on the very young and the very old.#expression:worried
<<showportrait CenterLeft Sekhmet>>
<<angerreaction Sekhmet>>
Sekhmet: Sue for peace? NO! That is not an option, put that out of your mind Meritamun. 
Sekhmet: <color=red>Egypt</color> is sovereign and must remain so at all cost. 
Sekhmet: What say your father <color=red>Ahmose</color>? What are his plans?
Meritamun: My Lady Sekhmet – every day I sit in the temple as your eyes and ears …. 
Meritamun: but nothing as of yet on the mind of <color=red>my father Ahmose</color> regarding the Eastern threat. #expression:worried
Sekhmet: You must find out faster, Meritamunn.
<<showportrait Left Bes>>
<<angerreaction Bes>>
Bes: Find out faster? 
Bes:How exactly can you ask a <color=red>CAT</color> to find out faster, unless by ‘out’ you mean mice? 
Bes:You’ve made her A DOMESTIC CAT!
Bes:<color=red>Joy and vermin control,</color> perhaps, but nobody is talking to CATS about platoon movements! 
<<showportrait CenterRight Thoth>>
Thoth: I really can’t say I didn’t tell you so <color=red>Sekhmet</color> my darling, viscous lioness, most hot of all the great feminine divines. 
Thoth: If you want <color=red>Egypt</color> winning wars it's really much more about playing the long game of bolstering the grain silos and harnessing the faith of a tamed, well-fed, civilised populace… 
<<angerreaction Sekhmet>>
Sekhmet: Again with the patronising advice, Thoth! 
Sekhmet: OUT with all of you! This plan is mine and I am not listening to any more blethering nonsense from anyone! 
Sekhmet: Meritamun keep at it – my blessings are upon you as you <color=red>guide your father</color>. 
Meritamun: Yes of course Lady Sekhmet. 
Thoth: Yes of course Lady Sekhmet. Anything for Lady Sekhmet. 
<<angerreaction Sekhmet>>
Sekhmet: <color=red>GAH!!!</color>

<<hideallportraits>>

<<fadetoday BackgroundManager>>
<<setgridsize 9 9>>
<<setpuzzle 𓐍𓆏𓏏:Path_A|𓃭𓆑𓈎:Path_B|𓂧𓁹𓆙:Path_C|𓋹𓁐𓋔:Path_D>>

<<showportrait Left Harwa>>
<<sadreaction Harwa>>
Harwa: Lost again at the races, rotten luck I suppose.
Harwa: Father is asking me to spend more time with <color=red>Nitiqret</color> but honestly I can’t stand that simpering baby.
Harwa: At least you are good company, <color=red>Temple Cat</color>. I wonder if you have a name? #expression:laughing
<<showportrait Right Cat_Meritamun>>
<<playsustainedsound CatPurr>>
Cat_Meritamun: *Purrrrrr.....*
Harwa: Oh I know, I'll ask -- would you like to be named <br> Sweet <b><size=+4>𓐍</size></b> Kitten <b><size=+4>𓆏</size></b> Beans <b><size=+4>𓏏</size></b> <br> Lioness <b><size=+4>𓃭</size></b> of the Ferocious <b><size=+4>𓆑</size></b> Desert <b><size=+4>𓈎</size></b> Sands <br> Mighty <b><size=+4>𓂧</size></b> Scourge <b><size=+4>𓁹</size></b> of Snakes <b><size=+4>𓆙</size></b> , or <br> ... Holy <b><size=+4>𓋹</size></b> Lady <b><size=+4>𓁐</size></b> of Thebes <b><size=+4>𓋔</size></b>? #wordsearch

<<if $selectedPath == "Path_A">>
    Harwa: Sweet Kitten Beans it is! #expression:laughing
    <<addgodaffinity Bes 1>>
    <<addhumanaffinity Chaos 1>>
<<elseif $selectedPath == "Path_B">>
    Harwa: Lioness of the Ferocious Desert Sands it is! #expression:laughing
    <<addgodaffinity Sekhmet 1>>
    <<addhumanaffinity Harwa 1>>
<<elseif $selectedPath == "Path_C">>
    Harwa: Might Scourge of Snakes it is! #expression:laughing
    <<addgodaffinity Bast 1>>
    <<addhumanaffinity Ptahhotep 1>>
<<elseif $selectedPath == "Path_D">>
    Harwa: Holy Lady of Thebes it is!#expression:laughing
    <<addhumanaffinity Nitiqret 1>>
    <<addgodaffinity Thoth 1>>
<<endif>>
Cat_Meritamun: \[... it's times like these that make me question my purpose here.\] #expression:puzzled

<<hideallportraits>>

<<setpuzzle 𓋀𓇼𓇓:Path_A|𓈍𓊽𓋔:Path_B>>


<<showportrait Left Ahmose>>
<<angerreaction Ahmose>>
Ahmose: The state of the treasury is an absolute disgrace – it is only in private prayer to you, oh Gods, I can fully, honestly admit this. 
<<sadreaction Ahmose>>
Ahmose: Harvests have been mediocre to awful in the last few years. 
Ahmose: There’s no chance of winning any kind of prolonged campaign against <color=red>the Persians</color>, because it would simply cost an amount of money we do not have.
<<showportrait Right Cat_Meritamun>>
<<playsustainedsound CatPurr>>
Cat_Meritamun: *Purrrrrr.....*
Ahmose: What I actually need is some sort of <color=red>distraction</color> to bolster our support here in <color=red>Thebes</color>. Here are the choices I see before me, either of which are expensive but probably less expensive than a war. Should I <br> Marry <b><size=+4>𓋀</size></b> Nitiqret to Harwa in a lavish <b><size=+4>𓇼</size></b> ceremony <b><size=+4>𓇓</size></b> or <br> Start building a new <b><size=+4>𓈍</size></b> temple <b><size=+4>𓊽</size></b> here in Thebes <b><size=+4>𓋔</size></b>? #wordsearch 
<<if $selectedPath == "Path_A">>
    Ahmose: Oh dear. I am not looking forward to bullying them into that. The things a father has to do for Egypt! Not that I’m questioning your divine will -- it was going to happen anyway and now is as good a time as any.
    <<addgodaffinity Bast 1>>
    <<addhumanaffinity Chaos 1>>
<<elseif $selectedPath == "Path_B">>
    Ahmose: Yes, yes... I shall start a magnificent new civic project, perfect pretext for a little extra taxation...
    <<addgodaffinity Thoth 1>>
    <<addhumanaffinity Nitiqret 1>>
<<endif>>
Cat_Meritamun: \[oh! Got to remember this and report back to Lady Sekhmet.\] #expression:standing

<<hideallportraits>>

<<setpuzzle 𓌱𓆙𓎟:Path_A|𓊪𓂝𓆈:Path_B>>

<<showportrait Left Nitiqret>>
<<angerreaction Nitiqret>>
Nitiqret: <color=red>Harwa</color> is being mean to me and I must seek vengeance.
<<showportrait Right Cat_Meritamun>>
<<playsustainedsound CatPurr>>
Cat_Meritamun: *Purrrrrr.....*
Nitiqret: What do you think? should I <br> Put <b><size=+4>𓌱</size></b> a snake <b><size=+4>𓆙</size></b> in his bed <b><size=+4>𓎟</size></b> or <br> Tell him he has to stop <b><size=+4>𓊪</size></b> throwing <b><size=+4>𓂝</size></b> dirt <b><size=+4>𓆈</size></b> at me in front of his friends to impress them? #wordsearch  

<<if $selectedPath == "Path_A">>
    Nitiqret: Oh! Good idea! I actually saw you catch a snake earlier… now where did you put it … #expression:happy
    <<addgodaffinity Bes 1>>
    <<addhumanaffinity Chaos 1>>
<<elseif $selectedPath == "Path_B">>
    Nitiqret: Oh alright. This is going to be difficult but since you are the wisest and most beautiful of cats I shall obey…where is that idiot brother of mine…
    <<addgodaffinity Bast 1>>
    <<addhumanaffinity Nitiqret 1>>
<<endif>>
<<angerreaction Cat_Meritamun>>
Cat_Meritamun: \[That idiot <color=red>Harwa</color>! Ugh! If we throw dirt at each other it only shows everyone else they can do the same to us!\] #expression:neutral

<<hideallportraits>>

<<setpuzzle 𓅨𓉻𓋔:Path_A|𓅱𓍯𓋔:Path_B>>


<<showportrait Left Amenhotep>>
Amenhotep: It’s not that I didn’t want to have <color=red>a child with Meritamun</color> – but the time wasn’t right and I was only trying to do right by her, for both of us.
<<sadreaction Amenhotep>>
Amenhotep: Now <color=red>Meritamun is dead</color> and I’m here, alone, without her.
<<showportrait Right Cat_Meritamun>>
<<playsustainedsound CatPurr>>
<<sadreaction Cat_Meritamun>>
Cat_Meritamun: *Purrrrrr.....*
Amenhotep: Our <color=red>child</color> has no way to come home to me with Ahmose’s spies everywhere. Should I <br> Trust <color=red>Neferura</color> to keep my son safe far <b><size=+4>𓅨</size></b> away <b><size=+4>𓉻</size></b> from Thebes <b><size=+4>𓋔</size></b>, or <br>Or send my own agents to seek out <color=red>Neferura</color> and bring her and the child <b><size=+4>𓅱</size></b> back <b><size=+4>𓍯</size></b> to Thebes <b><size=+4>𓋔</size></b>? #wordsearch
<<if $selectedPath == "Path_A">>
    Amenhotep: Yes, that's probably the wiser option, his safety should be my main concern.
    <<addgodaffinity Thoth 1>>
    <<addhumanaffinity Ptahhotep 1>>
<<elseif $selectedPath == "Path_B">>
    Amenhotep: It would be so good to have a small piece of <color=red>Meritamun</color> here with me.
    <<addgodaffinity Bast 1>>
    <<addhumanaffinity Chaos 1>>
<<endif>>
Cat_Meritamun: \[ I have a <color=red>son</color>... and <color=red>he lives?!?!</color>\] #expression:puzzled
<<hideallportraits>>
<<fadetonight BackgroundManager>>
Narrator: END OF CHAPTER 1
<<checkending>>

